    {
      "id": "4ce39eacd683103a024968d7f866d7090220adce",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3223020757,
          "type": null,
          "body": "My understanding of the C23 standard (first draft of the next standard [here](https://open-std.org/JTC1/SC22/WG14/www/docs/n3220.pdf) is that 7.22 **Integer types <stdint.h>** states\n\n> None of the types shall be defined as a synonym for a bit-precise integer type.\n\nWhich means we don't have to worry that the \"exact-width integer types\" (`uint32_t` and the rest) are typedefs for one of the new C23 `_BitInt()` \"bit-precise integer types\" (which do not undergo integer promotion, and presumably hence why they are excluded from the checked integer arithmetic.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2026-04-05T19:29:00.343Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-05T19:29:00.343Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 470724135,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 24211,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3faf02a07389d39c577215e22de5cebf0f726209",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 3223044307,
          "type": null,
          "body": "OK, so \"bit-precise integer type\" is a C23 neologism, distinct from C99 *et seq*'s \"exact-width integer type\"; for one thing, I guess you could have `_BitInt(17)`, but there probably ain't no `uint17_t`, and there's also the \"we really mean *N* bits, we don't promote values up\" part.\n\nSo I guess `ckd_sub()` might be able to handle `uint`*N*`_t` type.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
